1. the approval screen shows the proposal and a token            -> shown OK
1. the approver asks to approve what was shown                   -> approved OK
2. the same request is sent again                                -> approved OK (replayed)
2. approvals recorded in the finding history after two sends        -> 1
3. whoever carries the action out asks: is it still approved?    -> valid=True OK
3. the evidence changed after the approval; asked again          -> valid=False NOT_IN_FORCE
4. approval of a proposal that was replaced after it was shown   -> refused PROPOSAL_CHANGED
4. the finding is still 'action_proposed', not approved
5. a person with no right to approve in the finding's project    -> refused NOT_FOUND
5. the same answer as for a finding that does not exist             -> True
6. a request with a field the contract does not have             -> refused REQUEST_MALFORMED
THE BOUNDARY BEHAVES AS THE CONTRACT SAYS in these six situations (builder test world; no independent review)

